            "confidence": "medium",
            "summary": "The real-estate skill kit is mostly coherent, but its helper tools allow unscoped local template file reads and writes, so it should be reviewed before installation.",
            "dimensions": [
              {
                "detail": "tools/ruleengine.py accepts absolute or existing paths for user templates and writes template names without path normalization, allowing user-supplied values to read JSON files or write .json files outside the intended my_templates directory. render.py also derives output paths from config-controlled identifiers without normalization.",
                "label": "Credentials",
